----------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity

O(n)

Reason

Every node is visited exactly once.

----------------------------------------------------

Space Complexity

O(h)

where

h = height of tree

Worst Case

O(n)

(Skew Tree)

Balanced Tree

O(log n)

----------------------------------------------------

Why Pass Vector By Reference?

Correct

vector<int>& ans

Reason

Every recursive call uses the same vector.

No copy is created.

----------------------------------------------------

If Passed By Value

vector<int> ans

Each recursive call creates a new copy.

Changes are lost after the function returns.

Copying also increases the time complexity.

----------------------------------------------------

Recursive Template

void dfs(TreeNode* root, vector<int>& ans)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return;

    // Work

    dfs(root->left, ans);

    dfs(root->right, ans);
}

